error[E0277]: `paginate` reads this expression as a closure, and its value is `Paging<_>`, which is not a closure
  --> tests/paging-forms/refused/a_macro_in_a_pattern.rs:64:22
   |
64 |             paginate match DESCENDING { yes!() => by_link(), _ => by_link() };
   |                      ^^^^^ a closure is needed here
   |
   = help: the trait `for<'a> FnMut(forms::Call<List>, &'a Answer<Page>)` is not implemented for `Paging<_>`
   = note: if the value is a pager, write `.into_fn()` after a `Paging<…>` (`by_cursor(…).into_fn()`) or `Paging::from_pager(…).into_fn()` around a pager of yours; or write the pager as a call or a path, alone or at each tail of a plain block, `if` or `match`
   = note: if it is not, it is neither a closure nor a pager, and `paginate` cannot use it
   = note: required for `Paging<_>` to implement `concord::__private::InferredPager<forms::Call<List>, _>`
